<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Haji Shah (Atabeg of Yazd)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 1319</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Haji Shah was the last ruler of the Atabegs of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yazd">Yazd</a>, a local dynasty in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a> overlordship. In 1319 he was defeated and driven out by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mubariz-al-din-muhammad">Mubariz al-Din Muhammad</a>, who took Yazd and made it the first base of the Muzaffarid dynasty, which later ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fars">Fars</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kerman">Kerman</a>.</p></div>
